node.doctext:
Every now and then i use something this in my code:
<code>
for ($foo) {
  when (/blah/) {...}
  when (/xyz/)  {...}
 ...
 }
</code>

Now this page [https://www.effectiveperlprogramming.com/2017/12/beware-of-the-removal-of-when-in-perl-v5-28/|Beware of the removal of when in Perl v5.28] tells that <code>when()</code> will be removed in perl 5.28, meaning that i would need to change such code. But on this page [https://perldoc.perl.org/perldeprecation.html|perldeprecation] there is nothing written about removing <code>when()</code> or marking it deprecated. Now, what is correct about the  <code>when()</code>?
